"""One existing enforcement-diligence owner; no library/homepage generation."""
from refresh_dscr_purchase_methods import refresh

BODY = '''<p class="lead">Neighbor complaints can put an STR permit at risk where applicable rules connect proven violations, nuisance findings, inaccurate applications or responder failures to enforcement. Before buying, investigate the actual property record and buyer permission path. A complaint, a warning, a determined violation and a final revocation are different events. An active seller permit does not answer all four questions, and good guest reviews do not resolve an open case.</p>
<p><a href="/apply/">Bring the property’s enforcement evidence and unresolved questions to an acquisition call</a>. BNB Accelerator assists within its contracted acquisition scope; the issuing authority and qualified counsel determine legal status, liability and remedies. This guide is an evidence workflow, not an opinion that a particular property can keep its permit.</p>
<h2>Read the controlling rule, not a complaint count</h2>
<p>The current <a href="https://www.nashville.gov/departments/codes/short-term-rentals/operation-rules-and-requirements">Nashville operation rules</a> illustrate the distinction. The city describes possible revocation upon determination of three violations of generally applicable ordinances or laws, or a finding of false or misleading application information. It also assigns guest-activity responsibility to the permit holder and requires the responsible party to answer calls throughout each rental period. This is a city-specific summary, not a nationwide threshold or a legal reading of any file.</p>
<p>The same page says ownership changes cancel a permit and prohibits permit transfer. Do not assume a clean seller history authorizes the buyer or that a sale erases unresolved issues. Obtain the current code, effective permit conditions and authority response for the address. Have counsel review notice, hearing, appeal and finality requirements; no appeal deadline or automatic stay is supplied here.</p>
<h2>Build a six-field enforcement acceptance register</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Evidence to retain</th><th>Buyer acceptance question</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Property and permit identity</td><td>Address, parcel, permit holder, dates and case identifiers</td><td>Are these records for this property and use, rather than a similarly named listing?</td></tr>
<tr><td>Allegation and rule</td><td>Complaint description, inspection record and cited provision</td><td>What was alleged and what was actually determined?</td></tr>
<tr><td>Case status</td><td>Notice, decision, closure, hearing or appeal documents and dates</td><td>Is an unresolved proceeding being described as closed?</td></tr>
<tr><td>Physical or operational correction</td><td>Accepted scope, completed work and required sign-off</td><td>Does the authority accept the correction, not just the seller?</td></tr>
<tr><td>Buyer consequences</td><td>Written authority response and counsel’s contract review</td><td>What remains relevant after sale, and is buyer permission available?</td></tr>
<tr><td>Responsible person and cash</td><td>Named payer, responder, deadline and cleared funding</td><td>Who must act before the purchase review window closes?</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>Request available records from the issuing authority through its official process and obtain the seller’s notices, communications and remediation documents with permission. A search returning no record is not certification of no complaints. Ask about record coverage, missing periods, pending matters and the date checked. Keep personal guest and neighbor information in appropriate private channels; the public decision worksheet does not need names, phone numbers or allegations about identifiable people.</p>
<h2>Work through a disputed parking file</h2>
<p>Hypothetical document review, not an actual client or Nashville case: the seller provides three incident references. Event A is a neighbor complaint with no finding shown. Event B is a parking notice with a supplied closure letter. Event C is a later notice awaiting a hearing. You do not have three proven violations merely because there are three references. Nor does the closed second event prove that the third is harmless or that none of the history can matter.</p>
<p>For each reference, request the underlying document and current status. Confirm whether the seller’s “closed” description matches the authority record, what conduct was found, and whether a decision is final or review remains. Ask counsel how the local counting rule treats these events. A quieter guest policy is not a substitute for an answer about existing proceedings.</p>
<p>Next compare proposed occupancy and guest parking with legally authorized capacity and actual access. Use the <a href="/blog/parking-occupancy-str-cap/">parking and occupancy-cap guide</a>; reducing a listing’s guest count does not automatically satisfy a required correction. Where a responder failure appears in the file, confirm the accepted duty and coverage through the <a href="/blog/local-contact-before-buying-str/">local-contact purchase guide</a>. Do not infer that hiring any manager cures the record.</p>
<h2>Fund corrections without treating a promised reimbursement as cash</h2>
<p>For a separate invented budget, assume $325,000 accessible funds and a $288,000 complete acquisition allocation, including $45,000 retained operating cash. The allocation excludes the newly identified enforcement-review work below. Outside margin is $37,000; the retained cash is already included and cannot also pay these bills without changing the plan.</p>
<p>Assume $1,500 independent file review, $2,400 accepted parking work and 28 days of incremental no-receipt carrying cost at $140 per day. The carry is $3,920; the additional allocation is $7,820, giving $295,820 total and $29,180 outside margin. These are assumed costs, not local fees, likely legal expenses or a predicted approval interval. Define which carrying costs are incremental and avoid charging amounts already in the original allocation twice.</p>
<p>If the seller promises to reimburse the $2,400 after closing, keep the gross $7,820 need until the reimbursement actually clears or counsel confirms an enforceable, available closing arrangement. A promise is not spendable funding. With a 60-day interval instead, carry is $8,400; adding the same $1,500 and $2,400 gives $300,300 total and $24,700 outside margin. This tests cash, not permission, liability or a probability of success.</p>
<p>No disputed fine is assigned to the buyer in this example. Identify who legally owes existing penalties, how any agreement allocates costs, and whether payment settles the proceeding. If unresolved liability prevents a defensible budget, stop assuming a complete price. A seller credit does not establish lawful operation. Use the <a href="/tools/first-str-purchase-budget/">purchase-budget worksheet</a> to date distinct bills and retained cash.</p>
<h2>Turn unresolved records into an actual purchase decision</h2>
<p>Proceed only when the buyer permission route, actual case status, accepted corrective work and funded operating plan meet your requirements. Reprice a viable acquisition for supported additional cost; negotiate valid protection or an extension if decisive evidence remains outstanding. Do not presume a due-diligence cancellation right, a hearing delay or an office backlog extends the executed contract. Reject an STR thesis dependent on unavailable permission or unauthorized immediate rental receipts.</p>
<p>Retain a dated decision memo listing accepted evidence, unresolved questions, responsible people and the next verification point. The <a href="/blog/str-license-renewal-calendar/">renewal calendar</a> handles future milestones; the <a href="/blog/airbnb-neighbors-and-noise/">neighbor/noise guide</a> handles incident prevention and response. Neither replaces an enforcement-file review. Keep the seller’s original representations and later corrections rather than overwriting the record.</p>
<p><a href="/apply/">Discuss the shortlist with its enforcement register and independently funded downside</a>. For <a href="/blog/buy-str-high-income-large-tax-bill/">high-income buyers</a>, deployable capital and a hoped-for tax benefit do not cure missing permission. BNB Accelerator is the publisher and interested acquisition-service provider. This is document-based educational analysis, not firsthand property testing or professional approval.</p>
<p class="small">Nashville primary operation guidance reviewed October 7, 2026; it reports a March 13, 2026 update. Verify current address-specific rules and records before acting. All case events, costs and intervals here are hypothetical. Not legal, tax, lending, insurance or personalized investment advice. No permit, transfer, resolution, opening date, deduction or return is guaranteed.</p>'''

FAQ = [
 ('Do three neighbor complaints automatically revoke an STR permit?', 'No universal complaint-count rule is assumed. Read the applicable ordinance and distinguish allegations, determined violations and final decisions. The property’s actual records and procedural requirements control.'),
 ('Does an active seller STR permit settle open complaint history?', 'No. Obtain available notices, decisions, closure and appeal records, confirm current status with the authority, and separately establish the buyer permission path.'),
 ('Can a seller reimbursement pay enforcement-related work before closing?', 'A promised later reimbursement is not cleared funding. Identify the actual payer, due date and counsel-approved arrangement; budget gross required cash until an offset is genuinely available.')
]
